  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light is incident at an angle $i$ on a glass slab of refractive index $\\mu$. The angla between reflected and refracted light is $90^{\\circ}$ Then, the relationship between $i$ and $\\mu$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "dEqrv",
      "text": "$i=\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mu}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "E4Sn8",
      "text": "$\\tan i=\\mu$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6xusN",
      "text": "$\\sin i=\\mu$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NPr6w",
      "text": "$\\cos i=\\mu$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As situation can be diagrammatically as below\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2015_phy_a16.png\">\r\n\r\nFrom law of reflection\r\n$$\r\ni=\\theta\r\n$$\r\nNow, $\\quad \\theta+r+90^{\\circ}=180^{\\circ}$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n\\Rightarrow \\quad i+r+90^{\\circ} &=180^{\\circ} \\\\\r\nr &=90^{\\circ}-i\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\nAlso, from Snell's law $\\frac{\\sin i}{\\sin r}=\\mu \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\sin i}{\\sin \\left(90^{\\circ}-i\\right)}=\\frac{\\sin i}{\\cos i}=\\mu$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\tan i=\\mu$",
    "image": null
  },
